From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ufs: discovery containment: skip device housekeeping writes on resume

With system suspend allowed (0059), every resume re-armed the device RTC
update work, the timestamp attribute and auto-BKOPS. Discovery containment
never configures these at probe and its query gate refuses the writes, so
each resume logged "failed to enable bkops -30" / "Failed to update rtc
-30". Skip them under CONFIG_SCSI_UFS_DISCOVERY_READ_ONLY, as probe does.

--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c	2026-09-26 21:51:35.637498352 +0200
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c	2026-09-26 21:51:35.651692749 +0200
@@ -10623,9 +10623,18 @@
 		ret = ufshcd_set_dev_pwr_mode(hba, UFS_ACTIVE_PWR_MODE);
 		if (ret)
 			goto set_old_link_state;
-		ufshcd_set_timestamp_attr(hba);
+		if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SCSI_UFS_DISCOVERY_READ_ONLY))
+			ufshcd_set_timestamp_attr(hba);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Discovery containment never sets up the device RTC, timestamp or
+	 * auto-BKOPS at probe, and its query gate refuses those writes; do not
+	 * re-arm them on resume either (they only fail with -EROFS).
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SCSI_UFS_DISCOVERY_READ_ONLY))
+		goto skip_device_housekeeping;
+
 	schedule_delayed_work(&hba->ufs_rtc_update_work,
 			      msecs_to_jiffies(UFS_RTC_UPDATE_INTERVAL_MS));
 
@@ -10638,6 +10647,8 @@
 		 */
 		ufshcd_bkops_ctrl(hba);
 
+skip_device_housekeeping:
+
 	if (hba->ee_usr_mask)
 		ufshcd_write_ee_control(hba);
 
